==Trivia==
*Shachiko's name may be derived from the two readings of the kanji 鯱: ''shachi'' ([[wikipedia:Orca|orca]]) and ''[[wikipedia:Shachihoko|shachihoko]]'' (a fearsome, fish-like monster that can swallow massive amounts of water with a single gulp and hold it in its belly); as well as 古 ''ko'' (old) and 子 ''ko'' (common suffix in female given names, such as [[wikipedia:Sachiko|Sachiko]]). Ironically, ''shachihoko'' statues were often placed on ancient rooftops to ward against fire, yet Shachiko inflicts the Curse effect, whose icon resembles a flame.
**Shachiko also sounds similar to 社畜 ''shachiku'' (an overworked and exploited employee; a wage slave), which may fit in with the work-related descriptions of [[Dolphina]] (oversleeps for work) and [[Kid Tappa]] (his girlfriend said he should get a real job).
*Shachiko's [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] type may be a reference to how orcas are known for their intelligence and adaptability, with highly developed communication, memory, hunting and problem-solving skills.
*Shachiko may have some connection to [[Golem Sunfish]], another aquatic [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy. Golem Sunfish was sealed to the ocean depths by a sage but resurfaced from the ocean floor, which is where Shachiko's Japanese description says it found the Sage stone it ate.
*Although Shachiko's Japanese description calls it a fish, orcas are cetaceans. This implies that Shachiko is not actually an orca, but a piscine species that superficially resembles one, possibly as a result of [[wikipedia:Convergent evolution|convergent evolution]] or some form of [[wikipedia:Mimicry|mimicry]]. The English version does not call it a fish at all.
*The term 古代魚 ''[[wikipedia:ja:古代魚|kodaigyo]]'' in Shachiko's Japanese description literally translates to "ancient fish", but can also be used as a general term for fish considered "[[wikipedia:Living fossil|living fossils]]" of the Paleozoic and Mesozoic periods, particularly [[wikipedia:Osteichthyes|bony fish]] such as [[wikipedia:Coelacanth|coelacanths]] (though it does not have a strict definition).
*Shachiko's spritesheet contains an unused blue motion blur effect likely intended to appear during its attack animation.

